.SH NAME
lst \- list items moved to the trash
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    lst [OPTION...] [PATH]
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
The \fBlst\fR command lists the files and/or directories which have been
moved to a trash folder. The output format is similar to \f(CW\*(C`ls
\&\-g\*(C'\fR with the deletion time tacked on the end in brackets.
.PP
Items are grouped by their date of deletion and parent directory, and
then sorted by name (ascending) and time of deletion (descending).
.PP
.Vb 3
\&    $ lst
\&    [today, /home/user]
\&    \-rw\-r\-\-r\-\-  1 409K May 23  2025 \*(AqMy account info.zip\*(Aq       [16:35]
\&
\&    [yesterday, /home/user]
\&    \-rw\-r\-\-r\-\-  1 411K Apr 16 15:21 \*(AqPeek 2026\-04\-16 15\-21.gif\*(Aq [09:28]
\&    \-rw\-r\-\-r\-\-  1 411K Apr 16 15:19 \*(AqPeek 2026\-04\-16 15\-21.gif\*(Aq [07:19]
\&    drwxrwxr\-x  5 4.0K Dec 11  2025  perl5/                     [07:53]
.Ve
.PP
The \f(CW\*(C`PATH\*(C'\fR argument filters the list of trash items and defaults to
the current working directory. It may refer to an item that was itself
previously moved to the trash.
.PP
.Vb 3
\&    $ lst /some/deleteddir
\&    [2026\-04\-25, /some]
\&    drwxrwxr\-x  5 4.0K Nov 11  2024  deleteddir                 [19:01]
\&
\&    [2026\-01\-11, /some/deleteddir]
\&    \-rwxrwxr\-x  5 4.0K Dec 11  2025  my\-file                    [15:42]
.Ve
.SH OPTIONS
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
.IP "\-\-all\-items, \-a" 4
.IX Item "--all-items, -a"
List all trash items from the \f(CW\*(C`PATH\*(C'\fR\-relevant trash folder. Equivalent
to using \f(CW\*(C`\-\-recursive\*(C'\fR (see below) from your \f(CW$HOME\fR directory or a
filesystem mount point.
.IP "\-\-all\-trash, \-A" 4
.IX Item "--all-trash, -A"
List all trash items from all known trash locations. Equivalent
to using \f(CW\*(C`\-\-all\-items\*(C'\fR at the top of each trash location.
.IP "\-\-interactive, \-i" 4
.IX Item "--interactive, -i"
Run in Terminal User Interface (TUI) mode to interactively select and
restore items.
.IP "\-\-trash\-paths, \-T" 4
.IX Item "--trash-paths, -T"
List known trash \fIlocations\fR instead of trash contents. Raises an
error if a \f(CW\*(C`PATH\*(C'\fR is provided.
.IP "\-\-recursive, \-R" 4
.IX Item "--recursive, -R"
Recursively list entries which were moved from \f(CW\*(C`PATH\*(C'\fR and below.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
Trash folder information may be read from \fR\f(CI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR\fI/rmwrc\fR or
\&\fI\fR\f(CI$HOME\fR\fI/.config/rmwrc\fR
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
rmw(1)
.PP
The freedesktop.org Trash Specification <https://specifications.freedesktop.org/trash/latest>.
